\details{
Only supervised learning is wrapped (catlearn itself marks unsupervised
SUSTAIN as early-stage), so the unsupervised threshold \code{tau} is fixed at
0. Predictions depend on trial order and on the model's own recruitment
history, so every method takes the whole trial sequence, and learning is
driven by true category feedback rather than by the model's responses.

Ties between equally activated clusters are broken by recruitment order
(\code{ties = "first"}) by default, not at random: random tie-breaking would
make the likelihood differ from call to call and break optimizers. Set
\code{ties = "random"} to match catlearn's current default.

SUSTAIN's decision consistency \code{d} is typically large, so predicted
probabilities are often near 0 or 1; \code{\link[=cm_loglik.sustain]{cm_loglik.sustain()}} floors them at
1e-10 so a single confident miss doesn't make the likelihood \code{-Inf}.
